     SUB('Wound and shot: "at almost the first volley General Reynolds fell dead, shot through the head" (Bachelder); shot through the head at the moment of Meredith\'s advance (Meade 1913); struck in the brain, the woods full of the enemy\'s sharp-shooters (Bates 1875); at the first volley from Archer\'s brigade he fell mortally wounded (Indiana 1913); struck in the back of the neck by a volley (Weld diary) and shot through the neck (staff officers, as told to Weld, letter published 1912)', 'documented', 'conflict', ['bach_head', 'meade_head', 'bates_brain', 'in_volley', 'weld_neck', 'weld_letter'], 'head, brain or neck; all are rifle fire (Bates names sharp-shooters), against Heth\'s shell'),
