     SUB('The 147th New York did not receive the order because Lt. Col. Miller was wounded as he received it', 'documented', 'supported', ['cut_147']),
     SUB('Davis\'s brigade (Mississippi and North Carolina troops), advancing along the north side of the pike, attacked Cutler\'s three regiments; the 76th New York on the right was outflanked by the more extended enemy line, and the 55th North Carolina, the extreme left regiment of Davis\'s brigade, pressed its flank and rear', 'documented', 'supported', ['ny1_davis', 'ny1_out', 'ny2_55'], 'narratives of 1900 (the commission volume and the 76th New York address); Cutler\'s report does not name the force on his flank'),
     SUB('Wadsworth, seeing the perilous situation of Cutler\'s three regiments on the right of the railroad, ordered them withdrawn to a position in the woods on Seminary Ridge', 'documented', 'supported', ['ny1_wad']),
